WEBVTT

01:38.780 --> 01:39.910
This tastes terrible.

01:40.370 --> 01:42.160
S-Sorry.

01:42.490 --> 01:44.580
The only good that came out of this

01:44.580 --> 01:47.410
was that I can now appreciate
the coffee my household staff brews.

01:47.410 --> 01:50.170
This tastes like stewed sea slugs.

01:50.710 --> 01:53.800
I'll ask Secretary Fujiwara
to show me how to brew coffee.

01:55.050 --> 01:57.510
<i>Fujiwara suddenly finds herself
in a tight spot.</i>

01:58.130 --> 02:00.760
<i>Shinomiya's sure in a horrible mood.</i>

02:01.430 --> 02:03.060
<i>Persona!</i>

02:03.060 --> 02:08.560
<i>Every one of us plays a different role
for other people, depending on what they seek.</i>

02:09.190 --> 02:11.520
<i>Who you are when you're with friends.</i>

02:12.060 --> 02:14.730
<i>Who you are when you're with a lover.</i>

02:14.730 --> 02:18.490
<i>Not to mention who you are online.</i>

02:20.490 --> 02:24.160
<i>All the more so if you're
a member of the Shinomiya Family.</i>

02:25.200 --> 02:29.420
<i>The upbringing she received
was positively spartan...</i>

02:29.420 --> 02:32.920
<i>so in order to shield her mind
from that environment,</i>

02:32.920 --> 02:36.170
<i>she has been known to frequently
produce robust personas.</i>

02:40.720 --> 02:45.220
<i>These masks, so deeply ingrained in her life,
can be so unyielding at times...</i>

02:47.180 --> 02:48.600
<i>that you would think...</i>

02:48.600 --> 02:53.110
<i>she was someone else entirely.</i>

02:54.440 --> 02:55.610
Shirogane...

02:56.070 --> 02:57.650
I mean "President"...

02:57.650 --> 03:00.280
Shall we discuss
what happened the other day?

03:00.280 --> 03:01.110
<i>Here it comes!</i>

03:01.530 --> 03:06.080
How would you define
our relationship, President?

03:07.040 --> 03:09.460
Student council comrades...

03:09.460 --> 03:11.460
doesn't sound at all inspiring.

03:11.870 --> 03:13.210
Friends...

03:13.210 --> 03:14.880
doesn't sound right, either.

03:16.170 --> 03:18.050
Since we've come this far...

03:18.050 --> 03:19.380
I'd say...

03:20.880 --> 03:23.680
that we're boyfriend and girlfriend...

03:23.680 --> 03:24.390
maybe.

03:24.680 --> 03:26.640
Boyfriend and girlfriend
is a bit far-fetched, isn't it?

03:26.640 --> 03:28.520
<i>Seriously?</i>

03:29.020 --> 03:31.520
One kiss, and you're acting
like my boyfriend?

03:32.100 --> 03:35.770
Only a child would believe
that a kiss makes you instant lovers.

03:36.070 --> 03:39.780
Well, not that I blame you
for getting ahead of yourself, President.

03:40.440 --> 03:44.280
After all, I've known from the start
that you had feelings for me.

03:45.410 --> 03:47.700
Who are you to talk, Shinomiya?

03:47.700 --> 03:49.660
What was your reason for kissing me?

03:49.660 --> 03:51.790
You did it because you like me, right?

03:51.790 --> 03:52.790
In that case...

03:53.080 --> 03:56.170
I wish you wouldn't make
such a commotion over a mere kiss or two.

03:57.550 --> 04:00.920
Please, I would kiss anyone
if I was in the mood.

04:01.670 --> 04:02.930
On that note...

04:02.930 --> 04:04.840
would you like to do it now?

04:06.010 --> 04:07.560
Kiss?

04:27.030 --> 04:29.700
What's this?
A man waiting for a kiss?

04:29.700 --> 04:30.870
How creepy!

04:30.870 --> 04:33.290
No, I was just... I thought...

04:33.870 --> 04:36.290
<i>I thought she was going to force
a kiss on me again!</i>

04:36.290 --> 04:40.800
<i>That kiss is carved
deep inside Shirogane's mind.</i>

04:41.260 --> 04:44.050
Hey... I know it was kind of...

04:44.050 --> 04:46.180
But you didn't have to hit me!

04:46.180 --> 04:47.390
I apologize.

04:47.390 --> 04:50.850
But it's the Shinomiya way
to discipline the indecisive by hitting them.

04:50.850 --> 04:51.810
Anyway...

04:52.140 --> 04:55.690
I don't see myself
wanting to date such a spineless man.

04:56.810 --> 04:59.060
We're done for today. Good night.

04:59.400 --> 05:00.360
Huh?

05:00.900 --> 05:01.570
Oh my.

05:02.110 --> 05:05.070
I was planning to call
for someone to pick me up...

05:05.360 --> 05:08.370
but apparently,
smartphone batteries drain quickly.

05:08.370 --> 05:10.160
Therefore, I shall walk home.

05:10.160 --> 05:13.080
Huh? Are you sure you should be
walking home alone at this hour?

05:14.660 --> 05:16.750
Then, what do you propose?

05:21.170 --> 05:23.590
<i>What's gotten into Shinomiya?</i>

05:24.420 --> 05:27.720
<i>I thought things were pretty great
until yesterday,</i>

05:27.720 --> 05:29.600
<i>but now she's saying
she doesn't want to date me.</i>

05:30.430 --> 05:32.850
<i>And here she is, walking home with me.</i>

05:33.270 --> 05:36.810
<i>And that cold look on her face... Like ice.</i>

05:36.810 --> 05:41.860
<i>It's like she's reverted to being the Shinomiya
who rejected everyone around her!</i>

05:42.150 --> 05:44.860
<i>Something happened! I just know it!</i>

05:45.360 --> 05:47.860
<i>Did her father give her a hard time
about studying abroad?</i>

05:47.860 --> 05:49.620
<i>Or maybe he's against her dating!</i>

05:50.370 --> 05:53.540
<i>Don't tell me she's going to announce
that she has a fiancé!</i>

05:53.540 --> 05:56.870
<i>Is that why she took this long
to tell me that she couldn't date me?</i>

05:56.870 --> 05:58.210
<i>Figure it out, Miyuki!</i>

05:58.210 --> 06:01.250
<i>Shinomiya's got to be sending
some kind of sign!</i>

06:01.250 --> 06:03.420
You men are certainly lucky.

06:04.920 --> 06:09.760
Even if you walk around with your hands
in your pockets like that, no one reprimands you.

06:12.640 --> 06:14.520
My fingertips feel frozen.

06:14.850 --> 06:19.020
<i>Shinomiya's sighing because
she's thinking about male privilege.</i>

06:19.020 --> 06:21.690
<i>In the Shinomiya household,
where they treat people like objects,</i>

06:21.690 --> 06:23.400
<i>one example of male privilege would be...</i>

06:23.690 --> 06:25.400
<i>Could it be a fiancé after all?</i>

06:25.400 --> 06:28.400
<i>Shirogane is quite agitated.</i>

06:28.780 --> 06:31.280
<i>Shinomiya, what is it
that you want me to do?</i>

06:31.910 --> 06:33.030
<i>Just tell me what you're feeling!</i>

06:33.030 --> 06:34.160
Really, it's so bitterly cold!
<i>Just tell me what you're feeling!</i>

06:34.160 --> 06:35.040
Really, it's so bitterly cold!

06:35.700 --> 06:39.000
It feels like my heart
is about to get frozen, as well!

06:39.000 --> 06:41.670
One of us seems to have
warm hands! How lucky!

06:44.420 --> 06:47.630
<i>Does that mean she wants me to rescue her
from the cold with my hands?</i>

06:48.130 --> 06:49.880
<i>This is Shinomiya's cry for help!</i>

06:50.380 --> 06:51.340
<i>I...</i>

06:52.220 --> 06:54.640
<i>I have to do something about this!</i>

07:01.230 --> 07:02.150
President...

07:04.320 --> 07:08.150
I see that you're not even capable
of escorting a girl home the proper way.

07:08.780 --> 07:10.650
How cute.

07:28.090 --> 07:29.670
So spineless.

07:37.930 --> 07:41.850
L-O-L... I say.

07:51.740 --> 07:54.030
You don't have to put my hair up today.

07:54.370 --> 07:55.450
Oh my.

07:55.740 --> 07:59.620
But is there still some of that perfume
my sister-in-law gave me?

07:59.620 --> 08:00.960
Oh my, oh my.

08:01.710 --> 08:03.750
84 sheep...

08:04.080 --> 08:06.710
85 sheep...

08:07.250 --> 08:09.960
86 sheep...

08:10.300 --> 08:12.720
87 sheep...

08:14.300 --> 08:17.220
88 sheep...

08:18.890 --> 08:19.930
Sheep...

08:20.270 --> 08:21.770
Sheep...

08:22.980 --> 08:24.270
One coffin...

08:24.270 --> 08:25.230
Coffin?

08:25.600 --> 08:26.020
Two coffins...

08:26.020 --> 08:27.270
Hey, what do you think
you're counting, President?
Two coffins...

08:27.270 --> 08:27.610
Hey, what do you think
you're counting, President?

08:27.610 --> 08:28.980
Three coffins...
Hey, what do you think
you're counting, President?

08:29.230 --> 08:31.030
What do you mean?

08:31.030 --> 08:33.030
I'm counting sheep.

08:33.030 --> 08:34.860
I didn't get any sleep last night.

08:34.860 --> 08:37.870
No, you started counting coffins
midway through!

08:37.870 --> 08:42.000
Please don't count anything that suggests
you won't wake up once you fall asleep!

08:42.290 --> 08:45.170
<i>Morning, two days before Christmas Eve.</i>

08:45.170 --> 08:48.000
<i>There are now cracks in Shirogane's heart.</i>

08:48.460 --> 08:49.670
<i>And no wonder.</i>

08:49.670 --> 08:52.130
<i>Just when he thought he'd finally
get to start dating Kaguya,</i>

08:52.130 --> 08:55.130
<i>thanks to the culture festival
and all its promise,</i>

08:55.380 --> 08:58.930
<i>Kaguya suddenly... uttered the words,
"I cannot date such a spineless man!"</i>

08:58.930 --> 09:00.760
<i>And as if that weren't enough...</i>

09:01.310 --> 09:02.600
<i>How cute.</i>

09:02.600 --> 09:04.390
<i>Trauma words!</i>

09:05.060 --> 09:08.900
<i>You can't blame him
for suffering a mental collapse.</i>

09:09.270 --> 09:10.900
Hello!

09:12.360 --> 09:13.190
Hey...

09:13.190 --> 09:15.950
You're wearing your hair straight, Shinomiya.

09:15.950 --> 09:18.320
You haven't done that
since you put makeup on me.

09:18.320 --> 09:19.910
Yes, I remember that day.

09:21.290 --> 09:24.580
I have my makeup kit with me today,
so would you care to do it again?

09:24.580 --> 09:26.750
Uh, no, I think I'll pass.

09:27.170 --> 09:28.880
Well, what a pity.

09:28.880 --> 09:29.500
<i>Huh?</i>

09:30.130 --> 09:32.000
<i>She's in a good mood today.</i>

09:32.420 --> 09:33.760
Morning, Shinomiya!

09:35.170 --> 09:36.510
<i>Huh?</i>

09:37.470 --> 09:38.140
Snub.

09:38.140 --> 09:39.510
<i>Why's she ignoring me?</i>

09:39.510 --> 09:42.600
About the Christmas party I'm throwing...

09:42.600 --> 09:43.270
Yes?

09:43.720 --> 09:44.180
First, a toast! Of course
it'll be with non-alcoholic drinks!

09:44.180 --> 09:46.770
Listen, didn't you think
Shinomiya was acting weird today?
First, a toast! Of course
it'll be with non-alcoholic drinks!

09:46.770 --> 09:48.690
Listen, didn't you think
Shinomiya was acting weird today?

09:48.690 --> 09:52.020
No. She was the same as usual with me.

09:52.270 --> 09:56.900
And I thought we could all have hot pot
before we all get into a Christmas-y mood!

09:56.900 --> 09:58.280
Sounds good to me.

09:58.860 --> 10:02.080
And she's acting
like her usual self with Fujiwara.

10:02.620 --> 10:05.660
If we're talking weird,
she was way weirder yesterday.

10:05.660 --> 10:08.290
Yeah, that was a sight to see, too.

10:10.880 --> 10:14.380
<i>I really need to talk to her again, properly.</i>

10:25.390 --> 10:27.060
Vice President Shinomiya...

10:27.890 --> 10:30.940
You're wearing perfume, aren't you?
That's against the rules.

10:30.940 --> 10:34.570
Oh my. It's only the slightest of dabs.
Your sense of smell is astounding.

10:36.530 --> 10:39.070
No. Take this as a gift from me, Iino.

10:39.070 --> 10:39.820
What?

10:40.530 --> 10:42.950
Don't you ever use perfume?

10:42.950 --> 10:45.410
Of course not. I never...

10:45.410 --> 10:47.830
Oh? But Christmas
is just around the corner.

10:48.580 --> 10:51.210
This is as good a time as any
for you to learn, is it not?

10:51.880 --> 10:53.710
Your body, Iino...

10:55.840 --> 10:58.220
smells so sweet.

11:00.760 --> 11:04.220
Perfume is fragrant
because it blends with your body scent.

11:04.220 --> 11:08.230
The nape of your neck is warm, so applying it
there will really bring out the aroma.

11:08.810 --> 11:11.730
As long as you apply it 30 minutes
before seeing the person you wish to conquer...

11:12.440 --> 11:15.230
your body temperature
will have done its job by then,

11:15.230 --> 11:17.230
and you'll be able to draw
that gentleman toward you.

11:17.990 --> 11:20.490
And now you're just as guilty.

11:23.410 --> 11:24.490
But...

11:25.200 --> 11:28.330
doesn't this smell like something
a middle-aged woman would wear?

11:28.660 --> 11:32.750
Like someone who's really pushy.
I don't think it's for high school girls.

11:33.040 --> 11:38.050
Wrong! As I explained earlier, a perfume's scent
changes with the passage of time.

11:38.050 --> 11:41.180
Yes, it's an acquired taste initially,
but after 30 minutes—

11:41.180 --> 11:41.880
Shinomiya...

11:42.220 --> 11:43.970
Even right now,
it doesn't smell at all like—

11:43.970 --> 11:45.260
Do you have a minute?

11:45.260 --> 11:48.640
It smells just like my middle-aged aunts.

11:50.140 --> 11:51.140
Shinomiya?

11:56.070 --> 11:57.780
Why are you running away, Shinomiya?

12:05.490 --> 12:06.620
Kaguya?

12:07.030 --> 12:08.040
Shinomiya...

12:15.000 --> 12:16.000
<i>Why?</i>

12:17.040 --> 12:18.500
<i>What did I do?</i>

12:18.750 --> 12:21.260
<i>What did I ever do to you, Shinomiya?</i>

12:24.550 --> 12:26.260
You can't get away from me now!

12:27.430 --> 12:29.180
Why did you run, Shinomiya?

12:29.180 --> 12:30.640
Don't come near me! Please!

12:31.730 --> 12:32.770
I'm telling you...

12:33.230 --> 12:35.770
Don't come any closer to me!

12:36.110 --> 12:38.110
<i>She hates me that much?</i>

12:38.110 --> 12:39.780
<i>Tell me...</i>

12:41.570 --> 12:42.610
<i>why.</i>

12:42.610 --> 12:44.280
<i>The answer is simple.</i>

12:44.570 --> 12:48.660
<i>Because it hasn't been 30 minutes yet
since Kaguya applied the perfume!</i>

12:49.240 --> 12:52.830
<i>With the passage of time,
perfume changes as follows.</i>

12:52.830 --> 12:56.380
<i>The perfume Kaguya has on
is renowned for its middle note!</i>

12:56.380 --> 12:59.920
<i>Immediately after applying it,
it smells somewhat old-lady-ish.</i>

12:59.920 --> 13:00.800
<i>But...</i>

13:01.300 --> 13:02.800
<i>at this very moment, it hits her!</i>

13:03.420 --> 13:07.640
<i>Thanks to that dramatic chase, her body temp
has surged. And she's sweating profusely!</i>

13:08.300 --> 13:10.310
<i>The middle note emerges
when the aroma evaporates,</i>

13:10.310 --> 13:13.560
<i>blending with the wearer's own scent
in the most optimal way. Also known as...</i>

13:14.100 --> 13:17.940
<i>"the heart note," which has now arrived!</i>

13:18.980 --> 13:22.110
Fine. From now on,
I'll keep my distance, Shinomiya.

13:22.110 --> 13:23.070
Come back here.

13:23.070 --> 13:24.030
What?

13:24.360 --> 13:26.070
- Where do you think you're going?
- Huh?

13:26.950 --> 13:29.200
But you just told me to get lost!

13:29.200 --> 13:30.830
You can stay now.

13:30.830 --> 13:32.580
Actually, you have to stay or else.

13:32.870 --> 13:35.580
<i>I have no clue about the female mind!</i>

13:36.250 --> 13:40.170
Hey, Shinomiya... Don't you think
you were acting strange yesterday?

13:40.170 --> 13:43.510
I was the same as always.
The one thing that comes to mind...

13:43.510 --> 13:47.590
is that perhaps I was suppressing
the absurd side of me that got a bit carried away.

13:48.390 --> 13:50.100
Carried away?

13:52.770 --> 13:56.390
Though I did make an outrageous
promise to study abroad,

13:56.390 --> 13:59.520
once I regained my composure
and gave it some serious thought,

13:59.520 --> 14:03.360
I realized that it was a decision
so horrific, it left me shaking.

14:06.200 --> 14:10.620
Then, was that kiss also something you did
because you were carried away?

14:10.950 --> 14:12.950
I suppose you could say that.

14:14.200 --> 14:18.830
You seem to be taking
that kiss extremely seriously,

14:18.830 --> 14:22.250
but for me, that's all
a kiss really amounts to.

14:23.090 --> 14:25.630
On that note, would you like
to do it right now?

14:29.220 --> 14:30.390
Kiss me?

14:31.050 --> 14:31.890
Huh?

14:36.230 --> 14:38.230
I could never do that!

14:38.690 --> 14:41.730
A kiss isn't something
you do so casually!

14:41.730 --> 14:44.730
If you're not feeling it,
there's just no point—

14:45.070 --> 14:47.280
Ow! Why'd you kick me?

14:47.280 --> 14:48.490
Pardon me.

14:48.490 --> 14:52.990
It's the Shinomiya way to kick anyone
who'd hold a kiss more sacred than they should.

14:53.490 --> 14:56.620
What the heck are you
so mad about? Just tell me!

14:56.620 --> 14:58.000
Well...

15:00.540 --> 15:03.460
You've been blowing me off,
you look more gloomy than usual,

15:03.460 --> 15:06.010
you're letting your hair down,
you resort to violence!

15:06.010 --> 15:08.340
And you smell so nice
like perfume, which you never use!

15:08.840 --> 15:10.590
I'm worried about you, okay?

15:12.510 --> 15:14.180
Did you say I smell nice?

15:14.180 --> 15:16.180
Yeah, I did! You smell amazing!

15:16.180 --> 15:18.850
And this has to be a first, right?

15:21.770 --> 15:23.730
If only you'd noticed
like you did just now...

15:24.360 --> 15:26.860
then I'd always be in a good mood.

15:28.690 --> 15:30.610
I know this is a real stretch...

15:32.410 --> 15:36.120
but last night, when you were going on and on
about how cold you were...

15:36.790 --> 15:39.500
you weren't hinting that you wanted
to hold hands, were you?

15:42.540 --> 15:45.170
And it's because I didn't hold your hand...

15:45.630 --> 15:46.880
that you're mad.

15:48.840 --> 15:50.260
Of...

15:51.180 --> 15:53.390
- Of course that's not what this is about!
- Shinomiya!

15:55.720 --> 15:57.390
Yeah, of course not.

15:58.680 --> 16:00.310
Now you realize?

16:07.190 --> 16:08.900
You want to consult me about love?

16:09.360 --> 16:11.950
Yes. As someone with a boyfriend,

16:11.950 --> 16:15.740
I thought that I could benefit
from hearing your opinions.

16:15.740 --> 16:17.660
Well, of course I don't mind.

16:20.910 --> 16:23.670
You're letting your hair down today, I see.

16:25.170 --> 16:28.920
It reminds me of when we were first-years.

16:30.590 --> 16:32.090
Back then, you...

16:32.680 --> 16:34.840
were known as "Kaguya the Ice Princess."

16:35.590 --> 16:38.600
So unapproachable... Everybody's idol...

16:38.600 --> 16:40.680
Mine included...

16:41.430 --> 16:45.860
Back then, she was attractive
in the same way as Maki during her tense moments.

16:48.400 --> 16:49.650
So, Kaguya—

16:49.650 --> 16:52.280
I've been wondering about this
for quite a while.

16:53.280 --> 16:57.320
You frequently change the way
you address me, do you not?

16:59.790 --> 17:03.370
You're the only one at this school
who's so informal with me.

17:03.370 --> 17:06.500
In fact, you address me
as if we've always been close.

17:08.750 --> 17:11.340
My apologies! That was
overly familiar of me, wasn't it?

17:11.340 --> 17:12.720
No, I don't mind.

17:12.720 --> 17:15.760
I'm sorry! I won't address you
so informally again, Miss Kaguya!

17:17.140 --> 17:18.760
I really don't mind.

17:24.100 --> 17:26.270
Are you serious, Miyuki?

17:26.270 --> 17:28.020
You want my advice about love?

17:29.190 --> 17:30.440
Yeah.

17:30.770 --> 17:33.030
I'd really like to learn
more about how girls feel.

17:33.320 --> 17:36.490
I see. So as long as she's a woman,
anyone will do.

17:36.490 --> 17:38.200
Don't put it that way!

17:38.200 --> 17:40.780
Well, if that's what you're after,
leave it to me.

17:41.120 --> 17:43.040
After all, I'm a master of romance.

17:43.040 --> 17:43.660
Huh?

17:45.660 --> 17:46.620
I'm kidding.

17:46.620 --> 17:47.750
You're kidding?

17:49.290 --> 17:53.710
Never once have I experienced
a successful romance.

17:53.710 --> 17:55.050
Look how blue the sky is.

17:55.630 --> 17:57.800
Damn, I asked the wrong person.

17:58.300 --> 17:59.390
So?

17:59.390 --> 18:00.050
So...

18:01.260 --> 18:03.430
what is it that you wanted to ask me?

18:03.430 --> 18:06.810
President has absolutely no clue
about my feelings for him.

18:07.390 --> 18:10.820
President has absolutely no clue
about my feelings for him.

18:11.110 --> 18:13.070
President has no clue about my feelings...

18:13.360 --> 18:15.320
President has no clue about my feelings...

18:15.320 --> 18:17.200
President has no clue—

18:18.780 --> 18:21.410
Are we talking about you and Shirogane?

18:21.410 --> 18:23.990
Yes, that's what I'm telling you.

18:23.990 --> 18:28.500
But normally, you'd start by saying,
"I have this friend who..."

18:28.500 --> 18:30.880
You're already well aware, aren't you?

18:30.880 --> 18:33.460
Meaning that any such pretexts
would be a waste of time.

18:33.920 --> 18:37.340
<i>Realizing how ineffective it is
to use the friend ploy! So impressive!</i>

18:37.720 --> 18:41.100
<i>Miss Kaguya,
you're 100 times smarter than usual!</i>

18:42.100 --> 18:45.470
Well, this is about a friend of mine, okay?

18:45.810 --> 18:49.940
The woman actually said this.
That she'd kiss anyone if she was in the mood.

18:49.940 --> 18:52.060
And then she asked,
"Would you like to do it now?"

18:52.060 --> 18:54.480
I mean, who says that?

18:56.150 --> 18:58.320
Actually, that sounds so sweet!

18:58.320 --> 19:00.990
I know exactly how that girl feels!

19:02.620 --> 19:05.450
So, she'd kiss anyone
as long as she was in the mood?

19:05.450 --> 19:08.750
Obviously, she's trying to hide her true feelings
behind those assertive words.

19:09.250 --> 19:10.250
True feelings?

19:10.830 --> 19:14.590
What she's really saying is,
"You're the only one I'd ever be in the mood to kiss."

19:14.590 --> 19:17.260
If you wanna dig even deeper,
what she's really trying to say is...

19:17.630 --> 19:19.720
I want President to kiss me.

19:21.510 --> 19:23.050
What am I supposed to do?

19:23.050 --> 19:25.850
I tried every which way
to make President kiss me,

19:25.850 --> 19:28.980
but so far, nothing's worked,
and I'm at the end of my tether.

19:29.350 --> 19:31.730
You want President... to kiss you?

19:31.730 --> 19:32.610
Yes.

19:32.980 --> 19:34.230
Kiss you, Miss Kaguya?

19:34.650 --> 19:35.860
That's exactly what I just said.

19:36.150 --> 19:37.110
But why?

19:37.490 --> 19:39.240
For someone who already knows,

19:39.570 --> 19:42.110
that's quite a mean thing to ask.

19:43.370 --> 19:45.530
Because I'm in love with President.

19:46.080 --> 19:49.120
What other reason could there be?

19:49.370 --> 19:50.620
Ka...

19:50.620 --> 19:52.080
Kaguya!

19:52.080 --> 19:53.880
Why are you back to addressing me
informally now?

19:54.420 --> 19:57.670
But... I can't believe
you owned up to it just like that!

19:57.670 --> 20:01.130
I've already acknowledged
my romantic feelings for him.

20:01.130 --> 20:02.550
Romantic feelings?

20:02.550 --> 20:05.760
If I'm in love with him,
isn't it only natural to want him to kiss me?

20:05.760 --> 20:07.890
I want him to hold me close
with those arms,

20:07.890 --> 20:10.600
and if he wants to go even further,
I'd probably say yes—

20:10.600 --> 20:13.020
I got it! I got it, okay?

20:15.520 --> 20:17.400
At any rate, if you want him to kiss you,

20:17.400 --> 20:20.530
then all you have to do is be honest with him
about your feelings, right?

20:21.030 --> 20:22.780
That, I cannot do.

20:22.780 --> 20:24.030
Why not?

20:25.660 --> 20:27.540
Whenever I'm in his presence...

20:28.740 --> 20:30.790
for some reason,
I can't help being perverse.

20:31.040 --> 20:32.790
I totally get it!

20:32.790 --> 20:36.790
That's just it! Being with the person you love
makes you act all hostile and aloof!

20:37.210 --> 20:40.800
Actually, does "hostile and aloof"
really explain that behavior?

20:41.300 --> 20:43.800
I've been making all kinds of efforts!

20:44.180 --> 20:47.180
Like repeating over and over how cold I was,
to get him to hold my hand!

20:47.470 --> 20:50.020
I mean, she's walking right next to me,
venting all the while!

20:50.310 --> 20:52.140
And today I even put on some perfume!

20:52.140 --> 20:53.770
Then she ran off like her life depended on it!

20:54.060 --> 20:56.400
The truth is, I'm too embarrassed
to even talk to him!

20:56.400 --> 20:58.020
When I said hello, she ignored me!

20:58.320 --> 20:59.780
Have some empathy!

21:00.230 --> 21:03.700
I'm asking you myself! Please try to have
some empathy for how she feels!

21:03.700 --> 21:05.780
She's almost at the breaking point herself!

21:05.780 --> 21:08.030
So please, try to be understanding!

21:08.330 --> 21:12.500
You know, this person
is the exact same type as me.

21:12.500 --> 21:15.210
I'm feeling so much sympathy for her,
it's downright scary.

21:15.210 --> 21:18.040
If you told me we were related,
I'd believe—

21:19.960 --> 21:21.050
Wait.

21:21.340 --> 21:24.970
Is this about you and Auntie Kaguya?

21:26.090 --> 21:28.350
I've had a feeling about you two for ages!

21:28.350 --> 21:30.260
How far have you gotten?

21:30.260 --> 21:32.060
What? No, actually...

21:32.430 --> 21:34.810
We shared a grown-up kiss
at the culture festival.

21:34.810 --> 21:36.060
- Whaaaaat?
- Whaaaaat?

21:36.060 --> 21:38.940
I thought we were friends,
but you've beaten me to the punch!

21:38.940 --> 21:41.070
I wish I hadn't found out!

21:41.480 --> 21:42.570
<i>A grown-up kiss!</i>

21:43.280 --> 21:44.650
<i>About 40 seconds.</i>

21:45.030 --> 21:47.320
<i>And now, the dots have been connected.</i>

21:47.660 --> 21:50.580
But... that kiss was a mistake.

21:50.910 --> 21:52.750
Are you sure about that?

21:52.750 --> 21:55.660
What was your first kiss like,
Miss Kashiwagi?

21:55.660 --> 21:58.080
Huh? You're making this about me?

21:58.960 --> 22:00.840
We were on our way home after a date.

22:01.300 --> 22:03.340
And while we were waiting
for the light to change...

22:05.670 --> 22:07.340
out of nowhere, he...

22:09.090 --> 22:10.850
I wish I'd never found out!

22:11.350 --> 22:12.890
That's quite lovely.

22:12.890 --> 22:15.730
But it was all of a sudden
in front of a mini-mart!

22:15.730 --> 22:17.850
There's nothing romantic about that.

22:17.850 --> 22:19.610
That's fine.

22:20.020 --> 22:25.110
I'd rather have an ordinary kiss
just like everyone else in this world.

22:27.740 --> 22:29.530
All I want...

22:30.870 --> 22:33.540
is an ordinary romance.

22:40.710 --> 22:42.130
I wonder...

22:43.710 --> 22:44.760
what Shinomiya...

22:45.670 --> 22:47.760
thinks of me.

23:10.110 --> 23:14.910
<i>Ice Kaguya is one of Kaguya Shinomiya's
many diverse sides.</i>

23:16.160 --> 23:17.410
<i>She is...</i>

23:17.410 --> 23:21.670
<i>the manifestation of the wariness
everyone has toward one another.</i>

23:21.670 --> 23:25.420
<i>At the same time, she is also
the cowardly heart of one who's in love.</i>

23:27.130 --> 23:28.920
But I love you.

23:39.230 --> 23:41.650
<i>Today's battle result...</i>

23:41.650 --> 23:43.770
<i>Kaguya Shinomiya...</i>

23:44.110 --> 23:45.940
<i>loses.</i>

23:46.190 --> 23:47.940
Miyuki's betrayed me!

23:48.490 --> 23:50.910
You're the only one for me, Yu!

23:50.910 --> 23:54.910
An unhinged person just threw herself into my
arms saying the weirdest things at the worst time!
